         \u2502\n\u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2534\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518\n[Estimate - sensitivity computed around base]\n\nStep 3-2 Multiples cross-check:\n- FY2026E GAAP-adjusted EPS: $5.47 [Actual - guidance midpoint, SBC\n  added back]. At $214.56: 39.2x forward adjusted P/E [Arithmetic]\n- FY2026E GAAP EPS (est. ~$4.30 after SBC + restructuring): ~50x\n  [Estimate]\n- FY2026E owner FCF/share: 253/58.6 = $4.32 [Arithmetic]. At $214.56:\n  49.7x owner FCF [Arithmetic]\n- Fair multiple for 8-10% grower with 25%+ owner FCF margin and wide\n  moat: 25-35x [Assumption - comparable quality compounders]. On\n  FY2027E owner FCF $4.88/share: fair value $122-171, midpoint $146.\n- EV/Sales FY2026E: 10.6x [Arithmetic]\n\nStep 3-3 Reverse DCF:\nTo justify $214.56, the company must grow revenue ~14% per year for a\ndecade (to ~$3.5-3.8B by 2035) at 32.5% terminal EBIT margin \u2014 with the\nSBC expense still taken out of margin. That is a 15%+ owner-FCF CAGR\nfor 10 years. The base rate for scaled software doing this is low\n(~30-40% for even 10% growth, lower for 14%). Reverse DCF verdict:\nEXCESSIVE relative to base rates.\n\nStep 3-4 Tornado \u2014 Top 3 value drivers:\n1. Revenue growth 2027-2030 (\u03c3 \u00b12pp changes IV by \u00b115%)\n2. WACC (\u03c3 \u00b11pp changes IV by \u00b112%)\n3. Terminal EBIT margin (\u03c3 \u00b12pp changes IV by \u00b18%)\nThese become Thesis KPIs in Section 8.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 3.5. SECOND-ORDER EFFECTS\n\nStep 3.5-1 Competitive response (-3 to +3): -2. SAP, Oracle, Blue Yonder,\nand Infor are all investing in cloud WMS (2025 Gartner MQ has 6 leaders\n[Estimate - Trace Consultants]). AI features will be copied within 18-24\nmonths. MANH's 18-time leader position is a lead, not a permanent gap.\n\nStep 3.5-2 Reflexivity: POSITIVE loop \u2014 high stock price funds SBC-based\ntalent retention, gives acquisition currency, and signals stability to\nenterprise buyers. NEGATIVE loop \u2014 if the stock corrects (as it did in\nJan 2025, -24.5%), services bookings historically wobble and attrition\nrisk rises. Currently the loop is constructive but fragile.\n\nStep 3.5-3 Customer behavior evolution: Early adopters (<25% of base)\nconverted. Mainstream adopters are slower, more price-sensitive \u2014 the\nEssentials mid-market tier addresses this [Actual - call]. As penetration\nrises, CAC rises and switching costs may compress for small clients.\nLTV/CAC and churn data ARE NOT DISCLOSED [Unconfirmed].\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 4. SCENARIOS (BAYESIAN)\n\nStep 4-1 Scenarios (probabilities sum to 100%):\n\u2500 BEAR (20%): Cloud decelerates to ~10% by 2028; services flat; license\n  shrinks faster; AI fails to monetize; services margin compression.\n  Revenue 2035: $1.43B; EBIT margin 25%; WACC 9.5%; TV g 2.5%.\n  IV \u2248 $70/share.\n\u2500 BASE (55%): Cloud sustains 16-22% through 2030; services +3%; EBIT\n  margin reaches 32.5% by 2033; WACC 9.2%; TV g 3.5%.\n  IV \u2248 $120/share.\n\u2500 BULL (25%): Cloud 25%+ through 2030; AI becomes a material add-on\n  (5%+ of revenue by 2029); EBIT margin 35%; WACC 8.5%; TV g 4.0%.\n  IV \u2248 $165/share.\n\nStep 4-3 Bayesian note: Prior = base rates (30-40% success for 10%+\ngrowth); evidence (RPO +23%, cloud +26%, 3 consecutive record bookings)\nraises likelihood. Posterior probabilities above reflect this update.\n\nStep 4-4 Expected value:\nEV = 0.20\u00d770 + 0.55\u00d7120 + 0.25\u00d7165 = $121.25/share [Estimate]\n50% CI: $95-140 | 80% CI: $70-165 [Estimate]\nNone of the three scenarios reaches the current price. The market's\nprice is OUTSIDE my 80% confidence interval.\n\nStep 4-5 Margin of safety: (121 \u2212 214.56)/121 = \u221277%. NONE.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 4.5. TIME HORIZON ARBITRAGE\n\nStep 4.5-1 Market implied horizon: The current price implies ~10 years\nof 14%+ growth or a 7-8% discount rate with SBC ignored. That is a\n5-10 year horizon with aggressive assumptions.\nStep 4.5-2 My horizon: 3-5 years. Spread: Market horizon (5-10y) minus\nmy horizon (3-5y) = 0-5 years. There is NO favorable arbitrage \u2014 the\nmarket is discounting results FARTHER and more optimistically than my\n3-5 year visibility supports. For a 3-5 year view, the stock needs a\nmaterial de-rating.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 5. CONVICTION & POSITION SIZING\n\nStep 5-1 Conviction Score (0-15):\n1. Business quality: 3/3 \u2014 wide moat, excellent financials\n2. Valuation attractiveness: 0/3 \u2014 39-44% above fair value\n3. Macro alignment: 1/3 \u2014 neutral-to-mild headwind\n4. Thesis clarity: 3/3 \u2014 measurable KPIs: RPO, cloud growth, margins\n5. Execution traceability: 2/3 \u2014 raised FY2026 guide, but Jan 2025\n   services guidance miss is a scar\nTOTAL: 9/15 \u2192 MEDIUM conviction.\n\nStep 5-2 Conviction decay: Applies if held long without confirmation\n(-1 per 6 months). At 9/15 now.\n\nStep 5-3 Sizing: Medium conviction \u2192 max 4-6% for a normal long. BUT\nvaluation is strongly negative \u2192 recommended weight = 0% for new money.\nIf an existing position exists: TRIM to <2%, or exit into strength.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 5.5. BEHAVIORAL & POSITIONING\n\n- Short interest: 5.38% of float; 2.42M shares; DTC 2.79; MoM -16.6%\n  (shorts covering) [Actual - vendor]. Moderate; not a squeeze.\n- Institutional ownership: 113.11% [Actual - vendor; implies leverage/\n  double counting]; very high crowding.\n- Insider ownership: 1.35% [Actual]; no cluster buying signals\n  [Unconfirmed].\n- Options positioning: not retrieved [Unconfirmed].\n- Sentiment: Stock near 52-week high ($220.59 vs $214.56). Analyst mean\n  target $207 and median $210 are BELOW the current price [Actual -\n  vendor]. The stock has roughly doubled from $119 low. Sentiment is\n  stretched \u2014 momentum now exceeds sell-side fair-value aggregation.\n- Crowding risk score: 10/15 (high institutional ownership, momentum\n  extension above analyst targets, high multiple). Position cap: -1pp.\n- Behavioral insight: Investors are extrapolating the +23% RPO and\n  +26% cloud growth into a decade-long compound; the base rate says\n  mean reversion is likely. The 24.5% stock collapse in Jan 2025 shows\n  how violently this stock re-rates when guidance breaks.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 6. PORTFOLIO FIT\n(No portfolio provided \u2014 framework assessment only)\n\n- MANH at fair value ($130) would be a high-quality core holding:\n  low correlation to cyclicals, defensive cash flows, no debt.\n- At $214.56, the position adds MATERIAL multiple-compression risk to\n  any portfolio. If rates rise 50bp (10Y \u2192 5.2%), fair value falls to\n  ~$110-130 (WACC 9.7-10%), and the stock could re-rate to 30-35x\n  adjusted EPS = $165-190 \u2014 a 10-25% downside before fundamentals\n  change.\n- If the portfolio already holds MANH, it is likely an oversized\n  winner; trim to original weight to control single-stock risk.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 6.5. KELLY SIZING\n\n- Bear (20%): -67% return (price $70 vs $214.56)\n- Base (55%): -44% return (price $120)\n- Bull (25%): -23% return (price $165)\nExpected return = 0.20\u00d7(-67) + 0.55\u00d7(-44) + 0.25\u00d7(-23) = -13.4 - 24.2 \n- 5.75 = -43.4%.\nKelly fraction for a LONG: 0% (negative edge). Kelly for a SHORT:\nnegative expected value after borrow costs + momentum risk; not\nrecommended. Position size: 0% new money. If held, this is a SELL.\n\nRisk of being wrong: If the market is right (SBC is NOT a real expense)\nand WACC is truly 8%, fair value is ~$200 \u2014 the stock is only 7% above\nthat. This \"market view\" requires accepting that $111M of annual SBC\ncreates no shareholder dilution or economic cost \u2014 a position the data\npack explicitly rejects.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 7. RISKS & CATALYSTS\n\nRisks:\n1. Valuation/derating: 49.7x owner FCF with 8-10% growth \u2192 PEG >2.3.\n2. Services stagnation: services +3% (50% of revenue) \u2014 the Jan 2025\n   miss is a live precedent.\n3. Cloud conversion fatigue: <25% of base converted; mid-market\n   competition (SAP, Oracle, Blue Yonder) intensifying.\n4. AI monetization uncertain: CEO unable to quantify AI revenue impact\n   for 2H 2027 [Actual - call].\n5. Legal/regulatory: Rosen Law, Bronstein Gewirtz investigations, class\n   action (Prime v. MANH) following Jan 29, 2025 -24.5% drop [Actual].\n   Outcome uncertain [Unconfirmed].\n6. FX: $9M YoY RPO headwind [Actual - call].\n\nCatalysts:\n1. RPO growth above 25% (momentum)\n2. AI-specific revenue disclosure/guide (would reframe bull case)\n3. Continued cloud revenue growth 24-26%\n4. Services re-acceleration to +5%+\n5. Buybacks at