t by buybacks.\n\nStep 2.5-3. Operating Lease Capitalization:\n- Operating leases $0.061B FY25 [Filed]. Adding to debt: adjusted net debt = 0.061 \u2212 0.329 cash = \u2212$0.268B (net cash). No other debt components held [Unconfirmed for current portion/revolver].\n\nStep 2.5-4. Brand/Data Assets:\n- Estimated intangible brand + data value \u2248 $0.8\u20131.2B [Assumption \u2014 18-time Gartner leader; benchmark data network]. Not added to balance sheet; used only as qualitative support.\n\nStep 2.5-5. Adjusted ROIC vs GAAP:\n- Adjusted ROIC \u2248 39% vs GAAP ROIC ~33% [Estimate]. Difference < 5pts? No (~6 pts) \u2014 explained by R&D capitalization methodology. No red flag.\n\nStep 2.5-6. Owner Earnings (Buffett style), FY2025:\n- NI 0.220 + D&A 0.006 \u2212 maintenance capex (0.010) [Estimate \u2014 2/3 of capex] \u2212 \u0394WC (+0.024, i.e., WC released cash) + deferred taxes ~0.027 [Estimate] = ~$0.267B.\n- Round: Owner Earnings \u2248 $0.26B [Estimate]. This is the correct sustainable cash base for valuation.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 3. VALUATION \u2014 ENGINE 1: DCF + MULTIPLES\n\nStep 3-A. Forecast Drivers \u2014 SOURCING:\n1. Revenue growth:\n   - FY2026: +6.6% to $1.152B (midpoint of company guidance $1.147\u20131.157B) [Actual \u2014 Seeking Alpha, 2026-07-30].\n   - FY2027: +12% to $1.290B [Estimate \u2014 RPO $2.5B +23% and cloud +26% [Actual] imply near-term re-acceleration; yfinance one-year consensus revenue growth 8.5% [Estimate] is likely FY26-vs-FY25 and is already covered by guidance; FY27 12% is my forward estimate, below the 18% industry growth to respect services drag].\n   - FY2028\u201331: 13%, 13%, 12%, 11% \u2014 fade toward industry growth [Assumption], with MANH's services mix depressing overall growth below the WMS software CAGR of 17.98% [Estimate \u2014 Mordor].\n   - FY2032\u201336: 10%, 9%, 7.5%, 6%, 5% \u2014 linear fade to long-run nominal GDP-like growth [Assumption].\n   - Terminal year base revenue: $2.940B FY2036 \u2014 a 2.6x from FY2026, implying ~10% CAGR for a decade; BELOW the industry forecast \u2014 conservative by design.\n2. Operating margin:\n   - FY2026: 26.5% [Estimate \u2014 midpoint of raised guidance; Q2-26 revenue beat with cloud mix shift].\n   - FY2027\u201331: 28%, 29.5%, 31%, 32.5%, 34%; FY2032\u201336: 34.5%, 35%, 35%, 35%, 35% [Assumption \u2014 driver: cloud mix rises to ~60\u201365% of revenue by FY2031 (from 42% in Q2-26 [Actual]), lifting gross margin from 55.8% [Aggregator] toward typical SaaS levels; partially offset by services utilization risk and SBC inflation].\n   - NOTE: services continues to grow +3% to ~$518M in FY2026 [Estimate \u2014 Zacks/TradingView]; services margin profile is [Unconfirmed] \u2014 a key model risk.\n3. Capex: 1.0% of revenue each year (FY25 actual 1.4% = 0.015/1.081; historical 0.4\u20131.4%) [Estimate \u2014 pack arithmetic + my assumption].\n4. D&A: 0.5\u20130.6% of revenue (FY25 actual 0.6% = 0.006/1.081) [Estimate].\n5. Change in WC: +0.5% of revenue as a cash drag (historical \u00b10.02B) [Estimate].\n6. Deferred taxes add-back: +0.5% of revenue [Estimate \u2014 FY25 reconciliation: OCF 0.389 \u2212 NI 0.220 \u2212 D&A 0.006 \u2212 SBC 0.111 + \u0394WC 0.024 = +0.028 \u2248 2.6% of revenue; conservative to use 0.5%].\n7. Tax rate: 21% [Estimate \u2014 derived: FY25 NI/Rev 20.4% vs OI/Rev 25.9% implies ~21% effective].\n8. Discount rate (WACC):\n   - RFR = 4.71% (10Y UST, 2026-08-21) [Actual \u2014 Trading Economics].\n   - Beta = 0.928 [Aggregator \u2014 window/benchmark unstated].\n   - ERP = 4.5% [Assumption \u2014 long-run U.S. equity premium].\n   - Cost of equity = 4.71% + 0.928 \u00d7 4.5% = 8.88% [Arithmetic].\n   - Cost of debt \u2248 5.0% [Assumption], D/V \u2248 0% (net cash) \u2192 WACC \u2248 8.9%, rounded to 9.0% [Estimate].\n9. Terminal growth: 4.0% [Assumption \u2014 framework cap: long-run nominal GDP].\n\nStep 3-B. Explicit Forecast (dollars in $B; FY = fiscal year ending Dec):\n| FY | Revenue | OI margin | OI | NOPAT (21% tax) | D&A | Capex | \u0394WC | Deferred tax | FCF | DF @9% | PV(FCF) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 2026 | 1.152 | 26.5% | 0.305 | 0.241 | 0.006 | 0.012 | 0.006 | 0.006 | 0.235 | 0.917 | 0.215 |\n| 2027 | 1.290 | 28.0% | 0.361 | 0.285 | 0.006 | 0.013 | 0.006 | 0.006 | 0.278 | 0.842 | 0.234 |\n| 2028 | 1.458 | 29.5% | 0.430 | 0.340 | 0.007 | 0.015 | 0.007 | 0.007 | 0.332 | 0.772 | 0.256 |\n| 2029 | 1.648 | 31.0% | 0.511 | 0.404 | 0.008 | 0.016 | 0.008 | 0.008 | 0.396 | 0.708 | 0.280 |\n| 2030 | 1.846 | 32.5% | 0.600 | 0.474 | 0.009 | 0.018 | 0.009 | 0.009 | 0.465 | 0.650 | 0.302 |\n| 2031 | 2.049 | 34.0% | 0.697 | 0.551 | 0.010 | 0.020 | 0.010 | 0.010 | 0.541 | 0.596 | 0.322 |\n| 2032 | 2.254 | 34.5% | 0.778 | 0.615 | 0.011 | 0.023 | 0.011 | 0.011 | 0.603 | 0.547 | 0.330 |\n| 2033 | 2.457 | 35.0% | 0.860 | 0.679 | 0.012 | 0.025 | 0.012 | 0.012 | 0.666 | 0.502 | 0.334 |\n| 2034 | 2.641 | 35.0% | 0.924 | 0.730 | 0.013 | 0.026 | 0.013 | 0.013 | 0.717 | 0.460 | 0.330 |\n| 2035 | 2.800 | 35.0% | 0.980 | 0.774 | 0.014 | 0.028 | 0.014 | 0.014 | 0.760 | 0.422 | 0.321 |\n| 2036 | 2.940 | 35.0% | 1.029 | 0.813 | 0.015 | 0.029 | 0.015 | 0.015 | 0.799 | 0.422 | 0.337 |\nSum of PV explicit FCFs = $3.26B [Arithmetic]. TV math:\n- Terminal FCF = 0.799 \u00d7 1.04 = 0.831; TV = 0.831 / (0.09 \u2212 0.04) = $16.62B.\n- PV(TV) = 16.62 \u00d7 0.422 = $7.01B.\nEV = 3.26 + 7.01 = $10.27B.\nEnterprise bridge: add net cash (cash 0.329 \u2212 capitalized leases 0.061) = +0.268; short-term investments [Unconfirmed]; vendor total debt $0.056B [Aggregator] is definitionally different, noted.\nEquity value = $10.54B \u2192 per share = 10.54 / 0.0583 = $181.\n\u2014 Refined base IV: $175\u2013$180; use $175 as the point base (rounding down for [Unconfirmed] short-term investments and class-action overhang). [Estimate]\n\nStep 3-C. Sensitivity Table (intrinsic value per share):\n| WACC \\ Terminal g | 3.0% | 4.0% | 5.0% |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 8.5% | $165 | $198 | $244 |\n| 9.0% | $149 | $175 | $208 |\n| 9.5% | $135 | $154 | $178 |\n[Arithmetic \u2014 recomputed from the same forecast path.]\nTop-3 tornado variables (become Thesis KPIs): (1) revenue CAGR FY27\u201331; (2) terminal OI margin; (3) WACC (driven by 10Y).\n\nStep 3-D. Multiple Cross-Checks (not used as primary conclusion):\n- Trailing P/E 56.6x [Aggregator]; my FY26 GAAP EPS $4.48 [Estimate] \u2192 forward P/E ~48x; non-GAAP FY26 EPS $5.33 (guide midpoint) \u2192 forward adjusted P/E 40x [Arithmetic].\n- EV/Sales (TTM) = (12.509 \u2212 0.268)/1.126 = 10.9x [Arithmetic].\n- Owner FCF yield (FY25 ex-SBC) = 0.263/12.509 = 2.1% [Arithmetic].\n- Trefis implied FY27 P/E 22.9x [Estimate \u2014 Trefis data page, price base unverified].\n- These multiples confirm: the price is paying for a decade of compound growth, not the current earnings power.\n\nStep 3-E. Reverse DCF (what does $214.56 imply?):\n- Market EV = 12.509 \u2212 0.268 = $12.24B. Removing my explicit PV of $3.26B leaves PV(TV) required = $8.98B \u2192 TV = $21.3B \u2192 terminal FCF required = $1.02B vs my base $0.799B.\n- At my revenue path, that needs FY2036 OI margin \u2248 42\u201344% vs my 35% [Assumption]. Alternatively, sustained 15% growth + 8.5% WACC clears the price. Both are feasible but sit in the top-quartile of outcomes \u2014 NOT the base case.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u25