tion]. |\n| BEAR | 20% | 4-5% | 26% | 9.5% | $95 [Estimate] | Recession defers warehouse projects; services utilization collapses; 10Y >5.2%; legal overhang persists. |\n| TAIL | 10% | 2% | 20% | 10.0% | $50 [Estimate] | Class action finds culpability; customer churn; AI-native competitor disintermediates Tier-2 WMS. |\n(Probabilities sum to 100%; base case is the single highest probability.)\n\nStep 4-3. Bayesian update: Prior (Layer 1.5) for sustained-growth company = ~30%; updated by RPO +23%, cloud +26%, Q1/Q2 2026 revenue beats [Actual] \u2192 posterior base case 45%, bull 25% [Assumption \u2014 subjective mapping of evidence].\nStep 4-4. Expected Price = 0.25\u00d7250 + 0.45\u00d7175 + 0.20\u00d795 + 0.10\u00d750 = $165.25 \u2248 $165 [Arithmetic].\nStep 4-5. Margin of Safety:\n- Base MoS = (175 \u2212 214.56)/175 = \u221222.6% \u2192 NONE.\n- EV MoS = (165 \u2212 214.56)/165 = \u221230.0% \u2192 NONE.\n- Judgment: NO MARGIN OF SAFETY AT T0.\n- 50% CI: $150\u2013$200; 80% CI: $95\u2013$250 [Estimate].\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 4.5. TIME HORIZON ARBITRAGE\n\nStep 4.5-1. Market implied horizon: At 56x trailing EPS and 40x forward adjusted EPS with 12% growth, the market is discounting 10\u201315 years of elevated compounding \u2014 i.e., it is pricing the BULL case as the base case [Estimate].\nStep 4.5-2. My horizon: 3\u20135 years. Spread = 3\u20135 \u2212 10\u201315 = \u22125 to \u221210 years. NO long-side arbitrage exists at T0. Short-side arbitrage could exist IF FY2027 guidance disappoints or services margins deteriorate, but shorting a wide-moat compounder with a $500M buyback is a poor ris