f breaches of fiduciary duty/alleged misrepresentations re: business and growth prospects [via PRNewswire/AccessNewswire, May-June 2026].\n\nStep 9-4. Killed Arguments (identified, then dismissed \u2014 with revival conditions):\n- KILLED: \"Cloud transition is complete, therefore the old services problem is behind us.\" REVIVAL CONDITION: services revenue still $518M in FY26 and ~46% of revenue; it can crater independently of cloud. Revive if services < 30% of revenue AND OI margin >30%.\n- KILLED: \"Gartner leadership (18x) guarantees pricing power.\" REVIVAL CONDITION: any Gartner MQ ranking slip to quadrant leader churn, or share loss to SAP EWM in Tier-1 deals.\n- KILLED: \"$500M buyback at $214 is a strong signal.\" REVIVAL CONDITION: buyback completed \u226580% within 12 months AND at price <$200; otherwise it is at the high end of the value band.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 10. AUDIT RESULTS\n\n- A. Methodology: PASS \u2014 archetype chosen before valuation; no DCF-only conclusion; multiples and reverse-DCF used as cross-checks.\n- B. Valuation audit: PASS \u2014 explicit 11-year cash-flow path, annually shown; terminal growth capped at 4%; SBC treated as a real expense in the DCF; pack-FCF adjusted.\n- C. Bias audit: PASS with caveat \u2014 my history as an analyst structurally favors software compounders; the negative-MoS result argues against that bias. Overconfidence check: 80% CI ($95\u2013250) is wide; Core variable (FY27\u201331 growth) is [Assumption], not [Actual].\n- D. Consistency: PASS \u2014 the TTM-to-FY2026 bridge reconciles (TTM 1.126 vs FY26 guide 1.152); FY2025 equity/cash/lease