n  margin = 10.4% CAGR for a decade (2.3x today). At WACC 7.0%/g 4.0%, price is\n  justified. Verdict on the reverse DCF: demand path is AGGRESSIVE; discount\n  path is UNREALISTIC (2.3% equity premium over a 4.71% risk-free). Market\n  needs both halves of the bull case to work simultaneously.\n\nTORNADO SENSITIVITY (\u00b11\u03c3) \u2014 Top 3 thesis KPIs:\n  WACC \u00b11.0pp (8.2%\u219410.2%):         IV $132 \u2194 $98  (\u00b1$17)\n  Terminal growth \u00b10.5pp (3.0\u21944.0%): IV $108 \u2194 $122 (\u00b1$7)\n  Terminal O-FCF margin \u00b12pp (25\u219429%): IV $108 \u2194 $122 (\u00b1$7)\n  \u2192 WACC is the dominant variable. Thesis KPIs = 10Y yield, revenue growth,\n  owner-FCF margin.\n\nSECTION 3.5. SECOND-ORDER EFFECTS\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n3.5-1 Competitive response (\u22123 to +3): \u22121. If MANH's AI agents demonstrably\n  cut warehouse costs, SAP (EWM), Oracle, Blue Yonder and K\u00f6rber will match\n  features within 12\u201318 months; AI is unlikely to be a durable differentiator\n  in WMS, only a table stake. Switching costs protect the installed base;\n  new-logo differentiation is at risk.\n3.5-2 Reflexivity: MIXED, slightly negative. High stock price funds generous\n  SBC (talent attraction \u2014 positive), but SBC at 10% of revenue is a real\n  shareholder cost; the buyback at 39x is a value-destroying loop if the\n  multiple normalizes. No funding dependency (net cash) \u2014 reflexivity is weak.\n3.5-3 Customer evolution: Early adopters (top-50 retailers) \u2192 mainstream via\n  new \"Editions\" (Essentials/Enterprise/Premier) packaging, expanding TAM to\n  mid-market [Estimate]. LTV/CAC should improve with land-and-expand; churn\n  structurally low (mission-critical). Watch: net-new-customer share of\n  bookings (25% in Q2'26 [Estimate]) \u2014 if it stays below 25%, growth is\n  conversion-driven and finite.\n\nSECTION 4. SCENARIOS (Bayesian)\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nPriors (Layer 1.5) \u2192 updated with evidence (RPO +23%, cloud +26%, win rate\n>70%, 2025 growth +3.7%, GAAP EPS \u22129% y/y in Q2'26) \u2192 posterior scenarios:\n\n  BEAR (25%): Retail capex recession + AI feature commoditization + rates stay\n  high. Rev CAGR ~4% to 2035 ($1.66B), O-FCF margin 22%, WACC 9.75%, g 2.75%.\n  TV = 0.364\u00d71.0275/0.07 = $5.34B; PV(TV) = $2.11B; PV(explicit) \u2248 $1.6B;\n  EV + NC = $3.96B \u2192 ~$65; blended with multiple-compression path (25x GAAP\n  FY28 ~$3.6) \u2192 BEAR PRICE \u2248 $90/share.\n  BASE (50%): Layer 3 path \u2192 BASE IV \u2248 $125/share.\n  BULL (25%): Cloud/AI attach + Editions TAM + sustained share gains. Rev CAGR\n  ~11% to 2035 ($2.97B), O-FCF margin 30%, WACC 8.0%, g 4.0%.\n  TV = 0.891\u00d71.04/0.04 = $23.2B; PV(TV) = $10.7B; PV(explicit) \u2248 $4.3B;\n  EV + NC \u2248 $15.3B \u2192 ~$250/share.\n  Probabilities sum = 100%; Base is the single highest-probability scenario \u2713.\n\nEXPECTED PRICE = 0.25\u00d790 + 0.50\u00d7125 + 0.25\u00d7250 = $148/share\n  50% CI: $105 \u2013 $160 | 80% CI: $80 \u2013 $240\nMARGIN OF SAFETY vs $214.56: (125\u2212214.56)/125 = \u221272% (base);\n  (148\u2212214.56)/148 = \u221245% (probability-weighted). Judgment: NONE (deeply\n  negative). Price is inside only the top edge of my 80% CI \u2014 i.e., the market\n  is paying the full bull case.\n\nSECTION 4.5. TIME-HORIZON ARBITRAGE\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nMarket implied horizon: at 39.2x forward non-GAAP EPS (12% grower), the price\ncapitalizes roughly FY2029\u20132030 earnings \u2014 i.e., the market is paying for ~4\u20135\nyears of flawless growth today.\nMy horizon: 3\u20135 years. Spread = 0 to +1yr, NOT >2yr \u2192 no horizon arbitrage at\nT0. Arbitrage only exists if a 7% discount rate is correct; at a 4.71% 10Y I\njudge it is not. This is a \"right company, wrong price\" case, not a timing\nedge.\n\nSECTION 5. CONVICTION & POSITIONING\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nConviction score (5 \u00d7 3 = 15):\n  Business quality:           3/3  (wide moat, excellent financials)\n  Valuation attractiveness:   1/3  (72% above base IV; 39x fwd non-GAAP)\n  Macro alignment:            1/3  (4.71% rates, hawkish hold = headwind)\n  Thesis clarity (KPIs):      3/3  (RPO, cloud %, owner-FCF margin, GAAP EPS)\n  Execution traceability:     2/3  (guidance accuracy high; GAAP dilution and\n                                    8% restructuring noise)\n  TOTAL: 10/15 \u2192 HIGH conviction \u2014 but in the NEGATIVE direction (overvaluation\n  is the thesis). Conviction decay \u22121 per 6 months unless evidence arrives.\nSizing guideline (for the long side): at negative MoS, NO weight is justified.\nIf held from a prior entry, position should be REDUCED toward 0\u20132%.\n\nSECTION 5.5. BEHAVIORAL & POSITIONING\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n  Short % of float: 5.38%, DTC 2.79 days, MoM \u221216.6% (shorts covering; no\n    squeeze setup) [Actual \u2014 pack Aggregator]\n  Institutional ownership 113% (13F double-counting; effectively fully\n    institutionally held; vulnerable to passive-flow reversal) [Actual]\n  Insider ownership 1.35%; no cluster buying visible [Actual/Unconfirmed]\n  Options positioning: not in our data [Unconfirmed]\n  Sentiment: price ~2% below 52-wk high, ~4% ABOVE sell-side mean target\n    ($207) [Actual]; stock +80% off the $119 low on an \"AI Active Agents\"\n    narrative while GAAP EPS fell 9% y/y in Q2'26 \u2014 classic narrative-price\n    divergence. MGMT ITSELF says AI subscription revenue \"will remain small in\n    the near term\" [Estimate \u2014 call].\n  Crowding risk score: 11/15 (quality + AI + momentum + index ownership).\n  \u2192 Position-size penalty: \u22121pp if a long were held; reinforces the\n  reduce/avoid stance.\n\nSECTION 6. PORTFOLIO FIT\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nWithout the actual book: MANH is a high-long-duration, rate-sensitive holding\n(beta 0.93 vendor; effective beta to QQQ-type stress ~1.2\u20131.4 [Assumption]).\nIn a portfolio with other growth/tech, it adds correlation, not diversification.\nIts best-fit role would be a \"quality compounder\" sleeve \u2014 but only at a price\nwith positive MoS. At T0 it fails the fit test on price alone.\n\nSECTION 6.5. KELLY SIZING\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nEdge = (EV \u2212 Price)/Price = (148 \u2212 214.56)/214.56 = \u221231%\nKelly fraction = edge / odds \u2248 NEGATIVE \u2192 optimal weight = 0% (or short, which\nI explicitly do not recommend \u2014 see Layer 9). Consistency check: Layer 5 would\nimply 8\u201312% if positive; Layer 6.5 says 0%; gap resolves because MoS is\nnegative \u2014 both layers agree on ZERO new money. (Gap rule satisfied: no long\nweight to reconcile.)\n\nSECTION 7. RISKS & CATALYSTS\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nRisks (to the LONG thesis \u2014 i.e., what breaks at this price):\n  1. Multiple compression: 39x fwd non-GAAP \u2192 28x = \u221229% price with ZERO\n     operating disappointment. 10Y >5.25% or a Fed hike accelerates this.\n  2. GAAP dilution persists: SBC 10% of revenue; GAAP EPS \u22129% y/y in Q2'26.\n  3. Growth stall: 2025 already printed +3.7%; retail capex cyclicality;\n     services guidance trimmed $4.5M on FX/timing [Estimate].\n  4. Conversion dependence: >40% of cloud bookings are on-prem conversions\n     from <25% of the installed base \u2014 growth is partly a migration, not all\n     net-new demand.\n  5. Legal overhang: Rosen, Bronstein Gewirtz & HBS investigations of\n     fiduciary duties/misrepresentations (announced ~May\u2013June 2026, after the\n     stock's volatility). Typical plaintiff-firm pattern; expected cost low,\n     distraction real [Unconfirmed].\n  6. Buyback engine slowing: cash $329M\u2192$186M, $225M authorization left vs\n     $137M/qtr pace \u2014 EPS support is finite.\nCatalysts (upside): AI attach monetization; Editions TAM expansion; Fed\n  pivot/cuts; continued RPO beats (guide $2.62\u20132.68B, +18\u201320%).\nPrimary catalysts at T0 are rate-driven, not company-driven.\n\nSECTION 7.5. CORRELATION-ADJUSTED RISK\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nCommon bear trigger with the rest of a growth-heavy book: rising REAL rates.\nMANH's 39x multiple is effectively a duration asset \u2014 it de-rates in the same\nepisode as QQQ/ARKK/long-duration software. Historical tail correlation to\ngrowth indices during 2022-type stress is high [Assumption \u2014 base rate].\nCVaR estimate (10% tail): 10Y \u2192 5.5% and multiple \u2192 25x fwd non-GAAP \u21d2\n  price \u2248 $137 (\u221236%) [Estimate]. Pairing MANH with rate-sensitive longs\n  increases portfolio CVaR, not decreases it.\n\nSECTION 8. MONITORING RULES\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nThesis KPIs (from tornado + thesis): (1) 10Y yield; (2) revenue growth;\n(3) owner-FCF margin (OCF \u2212 capex \u2212 SBC)/revenue.\nTripwires triggering re-evaluation:\n  \u2022 Revenue growth <5% for 2 consecutive quarters\n  \u2022 RPO growth <10% y/y (guide is +18\u201320%)\n  \u2022 Cloud revenue growth <20%\n  \u2022 SBC >12% of revenue, or GAAP EPS declining 3+ consecutive quarters\n  \u2022 Adjusted op margin <32% (guide 35.1%)\n  \u2022 Win rate <60% or net-new-customer share <20% of bookings\n  \u2022 10Y >5.25% (mechanically cut fair value ~15\u201320%)\n  \u2022 Legal investigation escalates to a filed securities class action\nRe-entry conditions (for the value view): price in $150\u2013165 zone with MoS\n  \u226520% vs base IV, or a reset of guidance growth to \u226510% with margins stable.\n\nSECTION 9. RED TEAM & ADVERSARIAL ANALYSIS\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nSHORT THESIS (5\u20137 bullets, same data):\n  1. GAAP EPS is DECLINING (\u22129% y/y Q2'26) while the stock trades at 39x\n     non-GAAP; the market is paying for SBC-adjusted earnings that real cash\n     flow (after SBC) does not support at 46x owner-FCF.\n  2. Implied discount rate \u22487.0% vs 4.71% risk-free = 2.3% equity premium \u2014\n     bond-like pricing for a retail-capex cyclical.\n  3. FY2025 grew only +3.7%; guidance +7.6%; the 13% CAGR is history.\n  4. WMS market ~$4.8B; MANH ~24% share; SAP/Oracle/Blue Yonder/K\u00f6rber can\n     match AI features; AI revenue explicitly \"small.\"\n  5. Maintenance \u221212% and license attrition mean ~1pt of \"growth\" is mix\n     arithmetic; services had to be trimmed in Q2.\n  6. Buyback support is finite (cash $186M, $225M auth vs $137M/qtr pace) and\n     was deployed at ~39x.\n  7. Plaintiff-firm investigations pending; even meritless, they tax the\n     narrative premium.\nLONG THESIS (bullets): 18x Gartner leader; >70% win rate; RPO +23% to $2.5B\n  (2.2x revenue visibility); cloud +26%; 56% GM / 35% adj-OM / 30% FCF margin;\n  net cash; AI agents 100% pilot\u2192subscription conversion; Editions expands\n  TAM; recurring revenue de-risks the model.\nLOGIC COMBAT: Long quality 6/10 vs Short price/rate math 7/10 \u2192 gap = 1 < 2\n  \u21d2 downgrade conviction: do NOT press a large short; the business is real and\n  momentum is with the long. This is why the execution opinion is\n  AVOID/REDUCE, not a conviction short.\nADVERSARIAL DATA: no Hindenburg-type report located; the Rosen/Bronstein/HBS\n  investigations are the adversarial items on record [Unconfirmed].\nKILLED ARGUMENTS (and when they revive): (a) \"RPO $2.5B guarantees growth\" \u2014\n  killed: 39% of RPO converts within 24 months and is already inside guidance;\n  revives if RPO growth re-accelerates >25%. (b) \"AI re-rating is durable\" \u2014\n  killed: mgmt says AI revenue small near-term; revives if AI attach reaches\n  >30% of new bookings with pricing power. (c) \"Quality deserves <8% WACC\" \u2014\n  killed at 4.71% risk-free; revives if 10Y <3.5% while quality persists.\n\nSECTION 10. AUDIT RESULTS\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u250