t of capital plus the\nSBC add-back. Both exceed the base rates for this industry.\n\nData quality: Good. SEC-filed financials (Tier 1) for 12 years; guidance\nand RPO figures from secondary reporting of company calls (Tier 2/3);\nno segment data [Unconfirmed].\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 1. MACRO CONTEXT\n\nStep 1-1 Macro variables (T0 = Aug 2026):\n- 10Y Treasury: 4.71% (Aug 21, 2026) [Actual - FRED/TradingEconomics]\n- Fed funds target: 3.50\u20133.75%; FOMC on hold at July 2026 meeting\n  [Actual - J.P. Morgan / Charles Schwab research notes]\n- Fed stance: Cautious/Neutral; Powell signaling reluctance to cut with\n  inflation above target; market prices only ~1 additional 25bp cut in\n  2026 [Actual - Polymarket odds via search]\n- DXY: ~98.9\u201399.8, weak/drifting lower [Actual - TradingEconomics 2026-08-25]\n- S&P 500: 7,677; VIX: 15.45 [Actual - vendor quotes]\n- Inflation: Above 2% objective (Fed's July 2026 statement) [Actual]\n- Credit spreads: Not retrieved [Unconfirmed]\n- Real rates: 10Y TIPS implied real yield not retrieved; nominally 4.7%\n  10Y with ~2.5-3% core CPI \u2192 real ~1.8-2.2% [Estimate]\n\nStep 1-2 Regime probabilities [Assumption - my synthesis]:\n- Goldilocks (low rates + growth): 15%\n- Reflation (high rates + growth): 35%\n- Stagflation (high rates + low growth): 30%\n- Recession (low rates + low growth): 20%\nTotal = 100%.\n\nStep 1-3 Enterprise macro sensitivity (-3 to +3):\n- Interest rate sensitivity: +2 (long sales cycles; customer IT budgets\n  are rate-sensitive)\n- Dollar sensitivity: +1 (FX was a $9M YoY headwind to RPO in Q2 2026;\n  weak dol