th partner-sourced deals up 4x [Actual/Estimate - company claims].\nDeviation from base rate is modest and supported. No red-flag re-check\nrequired (success prob < 1.5x base rate).\n\nStep 1.5-3 Base rate shock: PASS \u2014 no excessive optimism embedded.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 2. BUSINESS QUALITY\n\nStep 2-1 Business understanding:\nMANH sells warehouse management (WMS), transportation, order\nmanagement, and inventory software to retailers, wholesalers, and 3PLs,\nincreasingly as cloud subscriptions. It makes money from recurring cloud\nfees (43% of revenue), implementation services (47%), and declining\nlicense/maintenance (10%). Understandability: Medium \u2014 the business is\nclear, but cloud transition accounting and the services margin dynamic\nadd complexity.\n\nStep 2-2 Moat score:\n- Intangible assets (brand/patents): 3/3 \u2014 18-time Gartner WMS Leader\n  [Actual - company claim], strong industry reputation\n- Switching costs: 3/3 \u2014 enterprise WMS deeply embedded; multi-year\n  contracts; migration costs are enormous\n- Network effects: 1/3 \u2014 limited; some AI/data network effects emerging\n- Cost advantage: 2/3 \u2014 cloud-native microservices architecture lowers\n  TCO vs legacy peers\n- Economies of scale: 2/3 \u2014 R&D scale on $1.1B revenue base\n- Regulatory barriers: 1/3 \u2014 low\n- Data moat: 2/3 \u2014 AI models trained on supply-chain datasets; growing\n  but not proprietary\nTotal: 14/21 \u2192 Wide moat.\nMoat direction: WIDENING \u2014 cloud share gains, AI differentiation,\npartner ecosystem expansion (4x partner deals) [Actual - company call].\n\nStep 2-3 Lynch classification:\nFast Grower (revenue +8-10%, cloud +24-26%, RPO +23%). However, the\nreported revenue growth UNDERSTATES the underlying cloud momentum \u2014\nand the stock price OVERSHOOTS it. Checkpoints: verify cloud durability\n(RPO is strong), watch services drag (services only +3%), watch license\nattrition.\n\nStep 2-4 Financial strength scorecard:\n- Revenue 3-yr CAGR (FY2022-FY2025): 12.1% [Arithmetic]\n- Revenue TTM growth: +4.2% (TTM $1.126B vs FY2025 $1.081B) [Arithmetic]\n- Operating margin FY2025: 25.9% [Actual]; 12-yr median 24.5% [Actual]\n- Net margin FY2025: 20.4% [Arithmetic]\n- ROE FY2025: 96.4% (vendor-computed; boosted by buybacks/equity base)\n- ROIC FY2025: ~118-174% [Estimate - see 2.5-5]\n- FCF margin (GAAP OCF - capex): 34.6% FY2025 [Arithmetic]; owner FCF\n  margin (after SBC): 24.3% [Arithmetic]\n- Net debt: Net cash $186M Q2 2026; zero debt [Actual - call];\n  operating leases $61M FY2025 [Actual - filing]\n- Interest coverage: N/A (no debt)\nVerdict: EXCELLENT.\n\nStep 2-5 Capital allocation scorecard:\n1. Buyback efficiency: 2/3 \u2014 consistent buybacks (share count -1.8%/yr\n   FY2025) but executed at elevated valuations ($200+ in 2025-26)\n2. M&A track record: 2/3 \u2014 limited M&A; no impairments but no evidence\n   of value creation >WACC\n3. Capex efficiency: 3/3 \u2014 capex just 1.4% of revenue; incremental\n   returns enormous\n4. Rationality of mix: 3/3 \u2014 reinvest in cloud/AI + return excess cash\n5. Guidance accuracy: 1/3 \u2014 Jan 2025 services guidance collapse caused\n   a 24.5% one-day stock drop [Actual - PR Newswire]; FY2026 raised\n   since (recovery underway)\nSubtotal: 11/15.\nInsider: Ownership 1.35% (no bonus). Recent 6-mo insider transactions:\n[Unconfirmed]. Adjusted: 11/15.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 2.5. INTANGIBLES-ADJUSTED FINANCIALS\n\nStep 2.5-1 R&D capitalization:\nR&D not broken out in this data pack [Unconfirmed]. Industry typical for\nenterprise software: 12-18% of revenue [Estimate]. I CONSERVATIVELY DO\nNOT capitalize R&D; the DCF already expenses it via operating margin.\nIf capitalized over 4 years, reported EBIT would rise ~$50-90M, but the\nadjusted ROIC is already so far above WACC that it does not change the\ninvestment conclusion.\n\nStep 2.5-2 SBC treatment \u2014 CRITICAL:\n- SBC FY2025: $111M = 10.3% of revenue [Actual - SEC filing]\n- SBC 5-yr CAGR (FY2020-FY2025): 27.5% [Arithmetic]\n- Owner FCF (OCF - capex - SBC) FY2025: 389 - 15 - 111 = $263M\n  [Arithmetic]\n- GAAP FCF (OCF - capex): $374M [Arithmetic] \u2014 OVERSTATES owner\n  earnings by 42%.\nThe FY2026 \"adjusted EPS\" guidance of $5.44-5.50 adds SBC back\n[Estimate - derived from GAAP EPS $3.60 + SBC/share $1.82]. This is the\nprimary source of market overvaluation.\n\nStep 2.5-3 Operating leases:\nOp leases $61M (FY2025) [Actual]. Adjusted net debt = -186 + 61 =\n-$125M (net cash of $125M) [Arithmetic].\n\nStep 2.5-4 Brand/data assets: Brand is real but not reliably\nquantifiable [Unconfirmed]. Skipped to avoid fake precision.\n\nStep 2.5-5 Adjusted ROIC:\nApprox invested capital = Equity $315M + leases $61M - cash $186M =\n$190M [Arithmetic, FY2025]. NOPAT (EBIT 280 \u00d7 0.80) = $224M [Estimate].\nAdjusted ROIC \u2248 118% vs WACC of 9.2%. GAAP ROIC similar. Gap from GAAP\nROE (96%) is modest. No 5pp+ discrepancy requiring explanation.\n\nStep 2.5-6 Owner earnings (Buffett):\nConservative: NI $220M + D&A $6M - maintenance capex $15M = $211M\n[Arithmetic]. Inclusive of working capital release: OCF $389M - capex\n$15M - SBC $111M = $263M [Arithmetic \u2014 includes +$52M WC inflow].\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 3. VALUATION (ENGINE 1: DCF + MULTIPLES)\n\nArchetype: B (Quality Compounder). Engine: Engine 1.\nRationale: Stable cash flows, high ROIC, no debt, wide moat. Not a\ncyclical, not an option-led story (AI is optionality, not the base).\nErrors if another engine used: Engine 4 would overvalue AI optionality;\nEngine 2 would misapply cycle normalization. No archetype transition \u2014\nthe license\u2192cloud transition is a business-model shift WITHIN archetype B.\n\nStep 3-1 DCF \u2014 explicit forecast:\n\nREVENUE FORECAST ($B):\n\u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u252c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u252c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u252c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510\n\u2502 FY  \u2502Revenue \u2502 Growth  \u2502 Source                                    \u2502\n\u251c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2524\n\u25022025A\u2502 1.081  \u2502   \u2014     \u2502 [Actual - filing]                         \u2502\n\u25022026