vendor]. The stock has roughly doubled from $119 low. Sentiment is\n  stretched \u2014 momentum now exceeds sell-side fair-value aggregation.\n- Crowding risk score: 10/15 (high institutional ownership, momentum\n  extension above analyst targets, high multiple). Position cap: -1pp.\n- Behavioral insight: Investors are extrapolating the +23% RPO and\n  +26% cloud growth into a decade-long compound; the base rate says\n  mean reversion is likely. The 24.5% stock collapse in Jan 2025 shows\n  how violently this stock re-rates when guidance breaks.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 6. PORTFOLIO FIT\n(No portfolio provided \u2014 framework assessment only)\n\n- MANH at fair value ($130) would be a high-quality core holding:\n  low correlation to cyclicals, defensive cash flows, no debt.\n- At $214.56, the position adds MATERIAL multiple-compression risk to\n  any portfolio. If rates rise 50bp (10Y \u2192 5.2%), fair value falls to\n  ~$110-130 (WACC 9.7-10%), and the stock could re-rate to 30-35x\n  adjusted EPS = $165-190 \u2014 a 10-25% downside before fundamentals\n  change.\n- If the portfolio already holds MANH, it is likely an oversized\n  winner; trim to original weight to control single-stock risk.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 6.5. KELLY SIZING\n\n- Bear (20%): -67% return (price $70 vs $214.56)\n- Base (55%): -44% return (price $120)\n- Bull (25%): -23% return (price $165)\nExpected return = 0.20\u00d7(-67) + 0.55\u00d7(-44) + 0.25\u00d7(-23) = -13.4 - 24.2 \n- 5.75 = -43.4%.\nKelly fraction for a LONG: 0% (negative edge). Kelly for a SHORT:\nnegative expected value after borrow costs + momentum risk; not\nrecommended. Position size: 0% new money. If held, this is a SELL.\n\nRisk of being wrong: If the market is right (SBC is NOT a real expense)\nand WACC is truly 8%, fair value is ~$200 \u2014 the stock is only 7% above\nthat. This \"market view\" requires accepting that $111M of annual SBC\ncreates no shareholder dilution or economic cost \u2014 a position the data\npack explicitly rejects.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 7. RISKS & CATALYSTS\n\nRisks:\n1. Valuation/derating: 49.7x owner FCF with 8-10% growth \u2192 PEG >2.3.\n2. Services stagnation: services +3% (50% of revenue) \u2014 the Jan 2025\n   miss is a live precedent.\n3. Cloud conversion fatigue: <25% of base converted; mid-market\n   competition (SAP, Oracle, Blue Yonder) intensifying.\n4. AI monetization uncertain: CEO unable to quantify AI revenue impact\n   for 2H 2027 [Actual - call].\n5. Legal/regulatory: Rosen Law, Bronstein Gewirtz investigations, class\n   action (Prime v. MANH) following Jan 29, 2025 -24.5% drop [Actual].\n   Outcome uncertain [Unconfirmed].\n6. FX: $9M YoY RPO headwind [Actual - call].\n\nCatalysts:\n1. RPO growth above 25% (momentum)\n2. AI-specific revenue disclosure/guide (would reframe bull case)\n3. Continued cloud revenue growth 24-26%\n4. Services re-acceleration to +5%+\n5. Buybacks at ~$275M YTD pace [Actual - call]\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 7.5. CORRELATION-ADJUSTED RISK\n\n- Primary macro risk factor: US 10Y yield (duration of the multiple).\n  A 50bp rise \u2192 ~10-15% fair-value decline [Estimate].\n- Common bear trigger with other high-multiple software holdings:\n  discount-rate shock. MANH's 0.928 beta understates its rate\n  sensitivity as a long-duration asset.\n- Tail correlation: In a 2022-style selloff (multiple compression),\n  MANH could fall 50-60% to $85-110 [Estimate \u2014 high multiple + beta 1].\n- CVaR (95%): -45% over 12 months [Estimate].\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 8. MONITORING RULES (if held)\n\nStep 7-1 Thesis KPI thresholds:\n1. RPO growth: MUST stay >15% YoY. Below 10% = thesis broken.\n2. Cloud revenue growth: MUST stay >20%. Below 15% for 2 quarters =\n   de-rate to $150.\n3. Owner FCF (OCF \u2212 capex \u2212 SBC): must grow >15% annually. If SBC grows\n   faster than revenue for 3 consecutive quarters, margin thesis breaks.\n4. EBIT margin: must reach 28% by FY2027, 30% by FY2029. Below 26%\n   GAAP in FY2026 = warning.\n5. Services revenue growth: Must not be negative for 2 consecutive\n   quarters.\n6. Legal: Any adverse judgment or expanded class-action scope \u2192 revisit.\n\nStep 7-4 Pre-mortem (2030):\nWhy did this stock fail? (1) Cloud growth fell to single digits as the\nconversion base saturates; RPO stopped compounding. (2) AI proved table\nstakes, not premium-priced; competitors bundled it. (3) Services\nutilization collapsed and SBC consumed margins. Early warnings: RPO\ngrowth <10%, cloud <15%, services negative, SBC >12% of revenue.\n\nStep 7-5 Decision journal:\nT0 price: $214.56. Fair value: $130. Key assumptions: 9.2% WACC, 3.5%\nterminal growth, SBC expensed, base revenue CAGR 7.5%. Red-team concern:\nthe market is ignoring SBC; my position is based on owner earnings\ndiscipline.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 9. RED TEAM\n\nStep 9-1 Short thesis:\n1. At 39x forward adjusted EPS and 50x owner FCF, the price implies a\n   decade of 14% growth \u2014 far above the base rate for $1B+ software.\n2. SBC ($111M, +10% of revenue, growing ~20%/yr) is added back in\n   \"adjusted\" EPS; GAAP EPS growth is far slower.\n3. Services (50% of revenue) grew only 3%; the Jan 2025 guidance\n   collapse showed the fragility of the services model.\n4. <25% of on-premise base converted to cloud; the remaining 75% are\n   the harder, price-sensitive customers.\n5. Six Gartner WMS leaders (SAP, Oracle, Blue Yonder, Infor, Infios)\n   are investing aggressively; AI features commoditize quickly.\n6. Legal overhang: securities class action + multiple investigations.\n7. At $214.56, the stock is ABOVE the sell-side mean target of $207.\n\nStep 9-2 Logic combat: Long logic quality: 6/10 (quality + RPO +\nmoat). Short logic quality: 7/10 (valuation + SBC + services).\nGap: 1 \u2014 within 2, so no additional downgrade. But the LONG case cannot\nwin on valuation; it depends entirely on a decade of flawless execution.\n\nStep 9-3 Adversarial data: Rosen Law Firm and Bronstein Gewirtz\ninvestigations [Actual - firm announcements]; Hagens Berman alert on\nFY2025 guidance [Actual]; Prime v. Manhattan Associates class action\n[Actual].\n\nStep 9-4 Killed arguments:\n- \"Quality compounders deserve 40x+\": Killed \u2014 quality is real, but\n  the price already embeds 35x+ FY2027 adjusted EPS. Valid only at\n  $150 or below.\n- \"AI will re-rate the stock higher\": Killed \u2014 CEO states no guidance\n  for AI revenue; too early. Would be revived if AI-specific revenue\n  exceeds $50M annually with disclosed pricing.\n- \"Buybacks support the stock\": Killed \u2014 buybacks at $200+ prices are\n  value-destructive; the $275M YTD repurchase funded partly by cash\n  that dropped from $329M (FY2025) to $186M (Q2 2026).\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 10. AUDIT RESULTS\n\nA. Methodology: PASS \u2014 Engine 1 appropriate; DCF + multiples + reverse\n   DCF all used; no single-method conclusion.\nB. Valuation: PASS \u2014 WACC derived (4.7% Rf + 1.0\u00d74.5% ERP); terminal\n   growth 3.5% \u2264 nominal GDP; SBC expensed per pack discipline.\nC. Bias: PASS with note \u2014 my bearish tilt was NOT the starting point;\n   the starting point was the market price, and the owner-earnings DCF\n   forced the conclusion. Cross-checked: using GAAP FCF (SBC add