e 15%+ persistence threshold. I deviate BELOW base rate, not above \u2014 justified by:\n  1. Services \u2248 46% of revenue ([Estimate] \u2014 FY26 services guided to ~$518M vs total $1.152B), growing slower than cloud;\n  2. MANH already commands ~23\u201325% share of the core WMS market ([Estimate] \u2014 $1.126B TTM revenue vs $4.77B WMS market), limiting share-gain headroom;\n  3. Mature base: $1.1B revenue scale means each percentage point requires ~$11M of annualized incremental revenue.\n- No base-rate shock check is triggered (my probabilities do not exceed 1.5x base rate).\n\nStep 1.5-3. Base-Rate Shock Check: PASS \u2014 the bull case (25% probability of 15% growth for a decade) sits at ~1.0\u20131.2x the persistence base rate and is supported by RPO +23% and cloud +26% [Actual].\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 2. BUSINESS QUALITY\n\nStep 2-1. Business Understanding (3 sentences):\n1. MANH sells mission-critical warehouse management (WMS), transportation management, and omnichannel commerce software to retailers, 3PLs, and manufacturers.\n2. It has completed a multi-year migration to a cloud-subscription model (Manhattan Active platform), where 42% of Q2-2026 revenue is cloud subscription and remaining RPO is $2.5B.\n3. Professional services (\u224846% of revenue [Estimate]) implement and support these systems; legacy license revenue is negligible and declining by design.\nUnderstandability: HIGH.\n\nStep 2-2. Moat Assessment + Dynamics:\n- Intangible assets (brand/leadership): 2 \u2014 18-time Gartner MQ WMS leader [Estimate \u2014 research brief].\n- Switching costs: 3 \u2014 WMS is embedded in daily warehouse operations; multi-year contracts; downtime is existential for customers.\n- Network effects: 1 \u2014 some data/benchmark network benefits, but not a classical two-sided network.\n- Cost advantage: 2 \u2014 scale economics in R&D and infrastructure.\n- Economies of scale: 2 \u2014 $1.1B revenue supports R&D scope small rivals cannot match.\n- Regulatory barriers: 0 \u2014 no regulatory license.\n- Data moat: 2 \u2014 anonymized fulfillment/benchmark data across installed base.\n- TOTAL: 12/21 = WIDE MOAT. Direction: STABLE-to-WIDENING (RPO +23%, cloud +26%, share gains in Tier 1; offset: Blue Yonder/SAP EWM/K\u00f6rber competition).\n\nStep 2-3. Lynch Classification:\n- STALWART with Fast-Grower characteristics: 12\u201313% historical growth, 25.9% operating margin, high ROE, pricing power. Checkpoints: consistency of double-digit growth (PASS \u2014 5-yr revenue CAGR 13.0% [pack]); margin stability (PASS \u2014 median operating margin 24.5%, latest 25.9%); balance sheet strength (PASS \u2014 net cash).\n\nStep 2-4. Financial Strength Scorecard:\n| Metric | Value | Source/Window |\n|---|---|---|\n| Revenue CAGR (3-yr FY22-25) | 12.1% | [Arithmetic] (0.767\u21921.081) |\n| Revenue CAGR (5-yr FY20-25) | 13.0% | [Arithmetic] (0.586\u21921.081) |\n| Operating margin FY25 | 25.9% | [Filed] |\n| Operating margin median (12 yrs) | 24.5% | [Arithmetic] |\n| Net margin FY25 | 20.4% | [Arithmetic] |\n| ROE FY25 | ~70% | [Arithmetic] NI/equity = 0.220/0.315 |\n| FCF margin FY25 | 34.6% | [Arithmetic] pack-FCF 0.374/1.081 |\n| FCF conversion (pack-FCF/NI) | 170% | [Arithmetic] |\n| Net cash (incl. capitalized leases) | $0.268B | [Arithmetic] (0.329 cash \u2212 0.061 leases) |\n| Interest coverage | n/a \u2014 no debt | [Actual] |\n| Structural rating | EXCELLENT | \u2014 |\nQualifying note: pack-FCF adds back SBC inside OCF; true owner FCF is pack-FCF minus SBC \u2248 $0.263B FY25 [Arithmetic]. The 170% conversion overstates distributable cash.\n\nStep 2-5. Capital Allocation Scorecard (0\u20133 each):\n1. Buyback efficiency: 2 \u2014 buyback authorization increased to $500M (from $100M) in March 2026 [Actual \u2014 StockStory]; shares \u22121.8% YoY, \u22121.9% CAGR [pack]; but buyback at ~56x trailing P/E is value-dilutive in hindsight.\n2. M&A track record: 2 \u2014 no major dilutive M&A visible; no impairment history in pack; conservative.\n3. Capex efficiency: 3 \u2014 FY25 capex $15M on $1.08B revenue; incremental ROIC far above WACC [Arithmetic \u2014 [Assumption] for incremental allocation].\n4. Rationality of mix: 3 \u2014 disciplined: R&D + cloud investment + buyback; no dividend.\n5. Guidance accuracy: 2 \u2014 Q1/Q2 2026 beats; but the Q4-2024/2025 guidance cut triggered the class action [Actual \u2014 AccessNewswire/PRNewswire].\n- Insider ownership: 1.35% [Aggregator] \u2192 no bonus, no penalty.\n- TOTAL: 12/15 = GOOD.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 2.5. INTANGIBLES-ADJUSTED FINANCIALS\n\nStep 2.5-1. R&D Capitalization:\n- MANH does not disclose a separate R&D line in our pack [Unconfirmed]. Estimated R&D \u2248 10% of revenue ($0.11B FY25) [Assumption \u2014 peer software norm].\n- Adjusted OI = 0.280 + 0.110 \u2212 0.0825 (4-yr amortization [Assumption]) = $0.308B.\n- Adjusted Invested Capital = equity 0.315 + unamortized R&D ~0.250 + leases 0.061 = $0.626B [Estimate].\n- Adjusted ROIC = 0.308 \u00d7 (1\u22120.21) / 0.626 \u2248 39% [Estimate] vs GAAP ROIC \u2248 30\u221235%. Gap explained by R&D capitalization.\n\nStep 2.5-2. SBC Treatment:\n- SBC FY25 = $0.111B [Filed]. Adjusted owner FCF = pack-FCF 0.374 \u2212 SBC 0.111 = $0.263B [Arithmetic].\n- Share count has declined 1.9%/yr despite SBC [Arithmetic] \u2014 dilution is fully offset by buybacks.\n\nStep 2.5-3. Operating Lease Capitalization:\n- Operating leases $0.061B FY25 [Filed]. Adding to debt: adjusted net debt = 0.061 \u2212 0.329 cash = \u2212$0.268B (net cash). No other debt components held [Unconfirmed for current portion/revolver].\n\nStep 2.5-4. Brand/Data Assets:\n- Estimated intangible brand + data value \u2248 $0.8\u20131.2B [Assumption \u2014 18-time Gartner leader; benchmark data network]. Not added to balance sheet; used only as qualitative support.\n\nStep 2.5-5. Adjusted ROIC vs GAAP:\n- Adjusted ROIC \u2248 39% vs GAAP ROIC ~33% [Estimate]. Difference < 5pts? No (~6 pts) \u2014 explained by R&D capitalization methodology. No red flag.\n\nStep 2.5-6. Owner Earnings (Buffett style), FY2025:\n- NI 0.220 + D&A 0.006 \u2212 maintenance capex (0.010) [Estimate \u2014 2/3 of capex] \u2212 \u0394WC (+0.024, i.e., WC released cash) + deferred taxes ~0.027 [Estimate] = ~$0.267B.\n- Round: Owner Earnings \u2248 $0.26B [Estimate]. This is the correct sustainable cash base for valuation.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 3. VALUATION \u2014 ENGINE 1: DCF + MULTIPLES\n\nStep 3-A. Forecast Drivers \u2014 SOURCING:\n1. Revenue growth:\n   - FY2026: +6.6% to $1.152B (midpoint of company guidance $1.147\u20131.157B) [Actual \u2014 Seeking Alpha, 2026-07-30].\n   - FY2027: +12% to $1.290B [Estimate \u2014 RPO $2.5B +23% and cloud +26% [Actual] imply near-term re-acceleration; yfinance one-year consensus revenue growth 8.5% [Estimate] is likely FY26-vs-FY25 and is already covered by guidance; FY27 12% is my forward estimate, below the 18% industry growth to respect services drag].\n   - FY2028\u201331: 13%, 13%, 12%, 11% \u2014 fade toward industry growth [Assumption], with MANH's services mix depressing overall growth below the WMS software CAGR of 17.98% [Estimate \u2014 Mordor].\n   - FY2032\u201336: 10%, 9%, 7.5%, 6%, 5% \u2014 linear fade to long-run nominal GDP-like growth [Assumption].\n   - Terminal year base revenue: $2.940B FY2036 \u2014 a 2.6x from FY2026, implying ~10% CAGR for a decade; BELOW the industry forecast \u2014 conservative by design.\n2. Operating margin:\n   - FY2026: 26.5% [Estimate \u2014 midpoint of raised guidance; Q2-26 revenue beat with cloud mix shift].\n   - FY2027\u201331: 28%, 29.5%, 31%, 32.5%, 34%; FY2032\u201336: 34.5%, 35%, 35%, 35%, 35% [Assumption \u2014 driver: cloud mix rises to ~60\u201365% of revenue by FY2031 (from 42% in Q2-26 [Actual]), lifting gross margin from 55.8% [Aggregator] toward typical SaaS levels; partially offset by services utilization risk and SBC inflation].\n   - NOTE: services continues to grow +3% to ~$518M in FY2026 [Estimate \u2014 Zacks/TradingView]; services margin profile is [Unconfirmed] \u2014 a key model risk.\n3. Capex: 1.0% of revenue each year (FY25 actual 1.4% = 0.015/1.081; historical 0.4\u20131.4%) [Estimate \u2014 pack arithmetic + my assumption].\n4. D&A: 0.5\u20130.6% of revenue (FY25 actual 0.6% = 0.006/1.081) [Estimate].\n5. Change in WC: +0.5% of revenue as a cash drag (historical \u00b10.02B) [Estimate].\n6. Deferred taxes add-back: +0.5% of revenue [Estimate \u2014 FY25 reconciliation: OCF 0.389 \u2212 NI 0.220 \u2212 D&A 0.006 \u2212 SBC 0.111 + \u0394WC 0.024 = +0.028 \u2248 2.6% of revenue; conservative to use 0.5%].\n7. Tax rate: 21% [Estimate \u2014 derived: FY25 NI/Rev 20.4% vs OI/Rev 25.9% implies ~21% effective].\n8. Discount rate (WACC):\n   - RFR = 4.71% (10Y UST, 2026-08-21) [Actual \u2014 Trading Economics].\n   - Beta = 0.928 [Aggregator \u2014 window/benchmark unstated].\n   - ERP = 4.5% [Assumption \u2014 long-run U.S. equity premium].\n   - Cost of equity = 4.71% + 0.928 \u00d7 4.5% = 8.88% [Arithmetic].\n   - Cost of debt \u2248 5.0% [Assumption], D/V \u2248 0% (net cash) \u2192 WACC \u2248 8.9%, rounded to 9.0% [Estimate].\n9. Terminal growth: 4.0% [Assumption \u2014 framework cap: long-run nominal GDP].\n\nStep 3-B. Explicit Forecast (dollars in $B; FY = fiscal year ending Dec):\n| FY | Revenue | OI margin | OI | NOPAT (21% tax) | D&A | Capex | \u0394WC | Deferred tax | FCF | DF @9% | PV(FCF) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 2026 | 1.152 | 26.5% | 0.305 | 0.241 | 0.006 | 0.012 | 0.006 | 0.006 | 0.235 | 0.917 | 0.215 |\n| 2027 | 1.290 | 28.0% | 0.361 | 0.285 | 0.006 | 0.013 | 0.006 | 0.006 | 0.278 | 0.842 | 0.234 |\n| 2028 | 1.458 | 29.5% | 0.430 | 0.340 | 0.007 | 0.015 | 0.007 | 0.007 | 0.332 | 0.772 | 0.256 |\n| 2029 | 1.648 | 31.0% | 0.511 | 0.404 | 0.008 | 0.016 | 0.008 | 0.008 | 0.396 | 0.708 | 0.280 |\n| 2030 | 1.846 | 32.5% | 0.600 | 0.474 | 0.009 | 0.018 | 0.009 | 0.009 | 0.465 | 0.650 | 0.302 |\n| 2031 | 2.049 | 34.0% | 0.697 | 0.551 | 0.010 | 0.020 | 0.010 | 0.010 | 0.541 | 0.596 | 0.322 |\n| 2032 | 2.254 | 34.5% | 0.778 | 0.615 | 0.011 | 0.023 | 0.011 | 0.011 | 0.603 | 0.547 | 0.330 |\n| 2033 | 2.457 | 35.0% | 0.860 | 0.679 | 0.012 | 0.025 | 0.012 | 0.012 | 0.666 | 0.502 | 0.334 |\n| 2034 | 2.641 | 35.0% | 0.924 | 0.730 | 0.013 | 0.026 | 0.013 | 0.013 | 0.717 | 0.460 | 0.330 |\n| 2035 | 2.800 | 35.0% | 0.980 | 0.774 | 0.014 | 0.028 | 0.014 | 0.014 | 0.760 | 0.422 | 0.321 |\n| 2036 | 2.940 | 35.0% | 1.029 | 0.813 | 0.015 | 0.029 | 0.015 | 0.015 | 0.799 | 0.422 | 0.337 |\nSum of PV explicit FCFs = $3.26B [Arithmetic]. TV math:\n- Terminal FCF = 0.799 \u00d7 1.04 = 0.831; TV = 0.831 / (0.09 \u2212 0.04) = $16.62B.\n- PV(TV) = 16.62 \u00d7 0.422 = $7.01B.\nEV = 3.26 + 7.01 = $10.27B.\nEnterprise bridge: add net cash (cash 0.329 \u2212 capitalized leases 0.061) = +0.268; short-term investments [Unconfirmed]; vendor total debt $0.056B [Aggregator] is definitionally different, noted.\nEquity value = $10.54B \u2192 per share = 10.54 / 0.0583 = $181.\n\u2014 Refined base IV: $175\u2013$180; use $175 as the point base (rounding down for [Unconfirmed] short-term investments and class-action overhang). [Estimate]\n\nStep 3-C. Sensitivity Table (intrinsic value per share):\n| WACC \\ Terminal g | 3.0% | 4.0% | 5.0% |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 8.5% | $165 | $198 | $244 |\n| 9.0% | $149 | $175 | $208 |\n| 9.5% | $135 | $154 | $178 |\n[Arithmetic \u2014 recomputed from the same forecast path.]\nTop-3 tornado variables (become Thesis KPIs): (1) revenue CAGR FY27\u201331; (2) terminal OI margin; (3) WACC (driven by 10Y).\n\nStep 3-D. Multiple Cross-Checks (not used as primary conclusion):\n- Trailing P/E 56.6x [Aggregator]; my FY26 GAAP EPS $4.48 [Estimate] \u2192 forward P/E ~48x; non-GAAP FY26 EPS $5.33 (guide midpoint) \u2192 forward adjusted P/E 40x [Arithmetic].\n- EV/Sales (TTM) = (12.509 \u2212 0.268)/1.126 = 10.9x [Arithmetic].\n- Owner FCF yield (FY25 ex-SBC) = 0.263/12.509 = 2.1% [Arithmetic].\n- Trefis implied FY27 P/E 22.9x [Estimate \u2014 Trefis data page, price base unverified].\n- These multiples confirm: the price is paying for a decade of compound growth, not the current earnings power.\n\nStep 3-E. Reverse DCF (what does $214.56 imply?):\n- Market EV = 12.509 \u2212 0.268 = $12.24B. Removing my explicit PV of $3.26B leaves PV(TV) required = $8.98B \u2192 TV = $21.3B \u2192 terminal FCF required = $1.02B vs my base $0.799B.\n- At my revenue path, that needs FY2036 OI margin \u2248 42\u201344% vs my 35% [Assumption]. Alternatively, sustained 15% growth + 8.5% WACC clears the price. Both are feasible but sit in the top-quartile of outcomes \u2014 NOT the base case.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 3.5. SECOND-ORDER EFFECTS\n\n3.5-1. Competitive Response: Blue Yonder (backed by Panasonic), SAP EWM (embedded in S/4HANA), K\u00f6rber, and Softeon shadow every Tier-1 deal. If MANH keeps winning at 20%+ cloud growth, expect aggressive 3-year pricing on transformational deals (\u22122 impact on margins by 2030). [Assumption grounded in Mordor's \"medium market concentration\".]\n3.5-2. Reflexivity: positive loop is real \u2014 $12.5B market cap, $500M buyback authority, SBC-based talent retention, and a strong acquisition currency (+1). A sustained de-rate would reverse the narrative, but the balance sheet (net cash $0.268B) prevents a downward spiral.\n3.5-3. Customer Behavior: early adopters (large omni-channel retailers/3PLs) are converting to Manhattan Active; the next cohort is mid-market and services-hungry. As penetration rises, implementation services intensity rises \u2014 capping margin expansion at ~35% OI rather than 40%+ [Assumption].\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 4. SCENARIO ENGINE (BAYESIAN)\n\nStep 4-1/2. Scenarios (all tag sources):\n| Scenario | Prob. | Revenue CAGR FY26-36 | OI margin FY36 | WACC | IV/sh | Rationale |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| BULL | 25% | 15% | 40% | 8.5% | $250 [Estimate] | AI add-ons lift ARPU; cloud >70% rev; services productivity via AI; class action dismissed; 10Y falls to 4%. |\n| BASE | 45% | 10% (table above) | 35% | 9.0% | $175 [Estimate] | RPO converts as modeled; services +3-6%; margins expand on mix; legal resolves at <$50M [Assumption]. |\n| BEAR | 20% | 4-5% | 26% | 9.5% | $95 [Estimate] | Recession defers warehouse projects; services utilization collapses; 10Y >5.2%; legal overhang persists. |\n| TAIL | 10% | 2% | 20% | 10.0% | $50 [Estimate] | Class action finds culpability; customer churn; AI-native competitor disintermediates Tier-2 WMS. |\n(Probabilities sum to 100%; base case is the single highest probability.)\n\nStep 4-3. Bayesian update: Prior (Layer 1.5) for sustained-growth company = ~30%; updated by RPO +23%, cloud +26%, Q1/Q2 2026 revenue beats [Actual] \u2192 posterior base case 45%, bull 25% [Assumption \u2014 subjective mapping of evidence].\nStep 4-4. Expected Price = 0.25\u00d7250 + 0.45\u00d7175 + 0.20\u00d795 + 0.10\u00d750 = $165.25 \u2248 $165 [Arithmetic].\nStep 4-5. Margin of Safety:\n- Base MoS = (175 \u2212 214.56)/175 = \u221222.6% \u2192 NONE.\n- EV MoS = (165 \u2212 214.56)/165 = \u221230.0% \u2192 NONE.\n- Judgment: NO MARGIN OF SAFETY AT T0.\n- 50% CI: $150\u2013$200; 80% CI: $95\u2013$250 [Estimate].\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 4.5. TIME HORIZON ARBITRAGE\n\nStep 4.5-1. Market implied horizon: At 56x trailing EPS and 40x forward adjusted EPS with 12% growth, the market is discounting 10\u201315 years of elevated compounding \u2014 i.e., it is pricing the BULL case as the base case [Estimate].\nStep 4.5-2. My horizon: 3\u20135 years. Spread = 3\u20135 \u2212 10\u201315 = \u22125 to \u221210 years. NO long-side arbitrage exists at T0. Short-side arbitrage could exist IF FY2027 guidance disappoints or services